  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Florida federal contract obligations totaled $22.3B in FY2026 to date. The state recorded 148,374 awards with an average award size of $150K. Obligations fell 31.4% year over year. Annual totals show a peak of $32.5B in FY25 and a decline to $22.3B in FY26. The Department of Defense obligated $15.1B in Florida, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs at $2.5B and the General Services Administration at $1.5B. LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION appears twice on the vendor list with $2.5B and $2.2B in obligations, and THALLE CONSTRUCTION CO INC obligated $1.9B. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing is the largest industry by obligations at $4.4B. Other major industries include Other Heavy and Civil Engineering Construction at $2.3B and Offices of Physicians (except Mental Health Specialists) at $1.8B. All figures above are contract obligations and reflect fiscal year to date totals.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What changed in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "Florida obligations totaled $22.3B in FY2026 to date, down 31.4% year over year. Annual obligations moved from $32.5B in FY25 to $22.3B in FY26. The Department of Defense continued to dominate buying with $15.1B in obligations. Award activity included 148,374 awards with an average award size of $150K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which sectors and vendors dominate federal buying in Florida?",
        "body": "Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing led industries with $4.4B in obligations. Other top industries include Other Heavy and Civil Engineering Construction at $2.3B and Offices of Physicians (except Mental Health Specialists) at $1.8B. LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION shows the largest vendor obligations at $2.5B and $2.2B, and THALLE CONSTRUCTION CO INC obligated $1.9B."
      }
    ]
